  "i18n": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Chime Dominoes",
      "concept": "Trace a path and dominoes line up along it; topple them and the chain climbs a scale to ring the bells. Sharp turns stop it, you can fork from the middle, and a ball carries the chain across water. Draw a run that reaches every bell with as few pieces as possible: build, topple, fix, and enjoy watching the cascade.",
      "howToPlay": "Trace from the green domino to place dominoes, press ▶ to topple and ring every bell. Start a trace on a domino to branch.",
      "libraryDecision": "Uses three.js: a cascade falling away from you reads best in 3D, and shadows and tilt show how far each piece reaches. Toppling uses my own simple deterministic model instead of a physics library, so curves and forks behave the same every try, which a trial-and-error puzzle needs.",
      "soundDecision": "No BGM. Each falling domino clicks and plays the next note of a pentatonic scale, so the chain itself becomes the melody; bells ring with layered harmonics as the reward."
    }
  },
